---
/**
 * The programme summary under the lockup in a footer's first column.
 *
 * SOURCE. The revised outreach readiness package, 29 September 2026: "A solid
 * deep-green footer holds the programme summary, distinct application/team
 * routes and legal/preferences links." Its footer reads "Build agentic systems
 * that hold up in production. / Practical building and review with Sunil
 * Mathew. 30 live hours plus independent work.", then an individual route and
 * a team route.
 *
 * Used by the three footers of the core journeys: `/` (BaseLayout), the tools
 * (ResourcesLayout) and the practice pages (SiteFooter). The consulting pages,
 * field notes and the policies keep their own footers: the package lists them
 * outside the core journeys, and a policy page stays free of promotion.
 *
 * The hours and the name come from facts.ts through PROGRAMME_SUMMARY, so
 * the footer and the page cannot state two different figures. The two routes
 * are text links: a footer is navigation, and a filled button there would
 * compete with the page's own action above it.
 */
import { POSITIONING, PROGRAMME_SUMMARY } from '../../data/resource-cohort-copy';
---

<p class="foot-positioning">{POSITIONING}</p>
<p class="muted">{PROGRAMME_SUMMARY}</p>
<p class="foot-routes">
  <a href="/#apply" data-cta="form" data-cta-placement="footer">Apply for the individual cohort <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  <a href="/programmes/enterprise/">Discuss your team’s need <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</p>

<style>
  /* Ivory on the dark footer is 13.43:1; on-dark-muted (the .muted line) is
     9.92:1. Both from ds/theme.css. */
  .foot-positioning {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--footer-ink);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .foot-positioning + :global(.muted) {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .foot-routes {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .foot-routes a {
    color: var(--footer-ink);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    /* The package asks for 44px controls; a text link in a list gets the
       height from its padding instead of looking like a button. */
    padding: 10px 0;
    margin: -10px 0;
  }
  .foot-routes a:hover {
    color: var(--footer-link-hover);
  }
</style>
